  "description": "The id-010 descriptor with `public_key` replaced by the 65-byte SEC1 uncompressed encoding (`0x04 || X || Y`, 87 chars) of the same P-256 point. RFC-AITP-0002 §3.3 permits only the 44-char compressed form for `p256`, so the descriptor is schema-invalid and is not byte-equal to the key in `sender.agent_id` (§3.2 step 2). The proof is the valid id-010 proof and the AID is in `trust_store`, so the key encoding is the only reason to fail. Receiver MUST reject with IDENTITY_FAILED.",
  "tags": [
    "security",
    "identity",
    "pinned_key",
    "p256",
    "key-encoding"
  ],
